# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# kungal API (apps/api) — LOCAL DEV env. Copy to apps/api/.env (godotenv loads it).
#
# Turnkey against the kun-galgame-infra dev stack. Onboarding is three steps:
#   1. cd ../kun-galgame-infra && pnpm dev:full
#      # Equivalent: docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml --profile full up -d
#   2. (optional) ./scripts/refresh-dev-db.sh        # real-shaped, desensitised data
#   3. cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env         # this file, then `pnpm dev`
#
# Every URL below points at the dev stack's host-network ports (identical to the
# prod ports 9277-9283). The OAuth client id + secret are the PUBLIC dev derivation
# (裁定 3) that refresh-dev-db bakes into oauth_clients — a client presenting the
# plaintext `dev-secret-<client_id>` authenticates. Details + the full port map:
# ../kun-galgame-infra/docs/dev-environment.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Server
SERVER_PORT=2334
SERVER_MODE=dev

# Database — kungal's own DB on the dev box's host Postgres (the dev source of
# truth; NOT a compose service). user postgres / password 191007 / db kungalgame.
KUN_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:191007@127.0.0.1:5432/kungalgame
DB_MAX_OPEN_CONNS=25
DB_MAX_IDLE_CONNS=10
DB_CONN_MAX_LIFETIME=300

# Redis (dev stack :6379)
REDIS_HOST=127.0.0.1
REDIS_PORT=6379
REDIS_PASSWORD=
REDIS_DB=0

# OAuth (KUN Galgame OAuth — dev stack :9277). client_id = the forum's registered
# client; client_secret = its public dev derivation. JWT_SECRET MUST match the dev
# stack's shared HS256 key (the oauth service signs access tokens with it).
OAUTH_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9277/api/v1
OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=4ed9bc99ec0a789a4796b83e22bd84c5
OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=dev-secret-4ed9bc99ec0a789a4796b83e22bd84c5
OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:2333/auth/callback
JWT_SECRET=kun-dev-jwt-secret-local-only-not-a-secret

# File storage (Backblaze B2 in prod). Uploads have moved to the artifact service
# below — the only thing left on this bucket is DELETING pre-cutover toolset
# resources whose type is still 's3'. The dev box holds no cloud credentials, so
# leave empty; deleting such a resource then just logs a warning.
FILE_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=
FILE_STORAGE_REGION=
FILE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
FILE_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=
FILE_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY=

# Search (Meilisearch — dev stack :7700). The key MUST equal the stack's
# MEILI_MASTER_KEY (docker-compose.dev.yml).
MEILISEARCH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7700
MEILISEARCH_KEY=kun-dev-meili-master-key-local-only

# NextMoe catalog galgame read surface (dev catalog instance :9281 or origin
# :19281; host base, no path suffix). Public reads and user writes go to /v2
# with Authorization: Bearer nmk_… . The only route still on the old family is
# the S2S claim-events feed, which has no v2 equivalent yet.
#
# The KEY is REQUIRED — the keyless-fallback valve was removed in wave 05, so an
# empty value now fail-fasts at config load rather than degrading to the legacy
# face. It must be the PLAINTEXT of a live `developer_api_keys` row for this
# app's OAUTH_CLIENT_ID (internal tier); only the sha256 hash is stored upstream,
# so a key that predates a dev-DB re-mint can never match and every galgame read
# answers 401 "未授权，请先登录" from the devapi middleware — not a session
# problem.
#
# Left EMPTY on purpose: there is no plaintext that stays valid, so anything
# checked in here would be a key that has already expired by the time someone
# clones. `devapi.GenerateKey` is crypto/rand — the old deterministic form
# `nm_test_dev<OAUTH_CLIENT_ID>` is retired, nothing seeds it any more, and a
# stale one left in .env is now the likeliest cause of that 401. A hand-seeded
# `nm_test_*` row is also wiped by every ./scripts/refresh-dev-db.sh.
#
# What survives a refresh is the app's own `*-internal-s2s` row, which is what
# prod authenticates with. Copy that plaintext out of the running container
# THROUGH A PIPE (never echo it — it lands in shell history and transcripts):
#
#   ssh kungal-neo 'sudo docker inspect <api-container> \
#     --format "{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}" \
#     | grep ^KUN_NEXTMOE_API_KEY=' | cut -d= -f2- >> apps/api/.env
#
# Say the trade-off out loud before doing it: that is a production s2s key with
# galgame:write/propose/nsfw sitting in a dev env, live against prod catalog if
# KUN_NEXTMOE_API_BASE is ever mispointed. The developer portal cannot replace
# it — a self-minted key forces nsfw=false and only catalog:read + galgame:read.
KUN_NEXTMOE_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:19281
KUN_NEXTMOE_API_KEY=

# NextMoe news face (/v2/news) — the 情报 stream republished from 月幕 Galgame
# and Galgame 批评, which the home page's "Gal 情报" tab reads.
#
# This is a SECOND key, not the one above: /v2/news is unauthenticated in
# preview but a news:read key is still the right leak boundary if you mint one.
# The catalog nmk_ must not be reused here.
#
# Leave it empty and /news answers 503 and the tab shows 情报服务暂时不可用;
# nothing else on the site is affected. KUN_NEWS_API_BASE defaults to
# KUN_NEXTMOE_API_BASE — set it only if the news face moves off that host.
KUN_NEWS_API_BASE=
KUN_NEWS_API_KEY=

# Catalog origin for the user-plane client (claims / proposals / playtime /
# cover votes). Public reads use KUN_NEXTMOE_API_BASE. Compose :9281 has no
# /v2; point this at the origin that serves /v2 (local infra :19281).
KUN_CATALOG_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:19281

# image_service public CDN prefix → the dev stack's read-through proxy (:9290),
# which serves the /<hh>/<hh>/<hash>.webp layout from local MinIO and falls back to
# the prod public CDN on a miss (so unseeded images still render). MUST match the
# wiki side's KUN_IMAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL exactly (no trailing slash).
KUN_IMAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9290

# image_service client credentials for direct uploads from kungal (galgame covers /
# screenshots — U2). Unlike the S2S clients below, these do NOT fall back to the
# OAuth creds — set them to enable /image/galgame (else it returns a clear "未配置"
# error). Reuse the dev OAuth client; the snapshot preserves its image_enabled bind.
KUN_IMAGE_CLIENT_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9278
KUN_IMAGE_CLIENT_ID=4ed9bc99ec0a789a4796b83e22bd84c5
KUN_IMAGE_CLIENT_SECRET=dev-secret-4ed9bc99ec0a789a4796b83e22bd84c5

# artifact service (dev stack artifact :9279) — large-file (toolset archive)
# upload/download. ClientID/Secret default to OAUTH_CLIENT_* when empty (app.go).
KUN_ARTIFACT_CLIENT_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9279
KUN_ARTIFACT_CLIENT_ID=
KUN_ARTIFACT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# community service (dev stack community :9282) — the UNCONDITIONAL backend for
# the galgame + resource (rating / website / toolset) comment areas over S2S. The
# legacy in-forum comment tables + routes were retired (charter step 06a), so
# comments are now always community-backed; there are no per-area feature flags.
# ClientID/Secret default to OAUTH_CLIENT_* when empty. Unconfigured (empty base
# URL / creds) = comments degrade gracefully: reads return empty pages, writes 503.
KUN_COMMUNITY_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:9282/api/v1/community
KUN_COMMUNITY_CLIENT_ID=
KUN_COMMUNITY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# trust & safety service (dev stack trust :9283) — report submission + inbound
# enforcement callbacks. S2S creds reuse OAUTH_CLIENT_*. Empty CALLBACK_SECRET =
# callbacks rejected (fail-closed), matching the dev stack (trust forwarding off).
KUN_TRUST_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9283
KUN_TRUST_SITE=kungal
KUN_TRUST_CALLBACK_SECRET=
# Two INDEPENDENT wave-1 moderation switches for topic/reply create+edit, both
# default off. CHECK = synchronous pre-write word-list gate (deny blocks / hold
# publishes+logs / fail-open ≤500ms); SCAN = async post-commit shadow scan
# (best-effort). Both also require the trust client to be configured. Flip to
# true only AFTER infra mints kungal's S2S client + the forum_topic/forum_reply
# kinds are registered.
KUN_TRUST_CHECK_ENABLED=false
KUN_TRUST_SCAN_ENABLED=false

# kungal-link-live-checker — the objective gate behind "report resource expired".
# Empty BASE_URL / API_KEY = the gate is OFF (legacy single-report-expires flow);
# no dev checker by default. CF_ACCESS_* only apply when a checker sits behind
# Cloudflare Access — leave empty for a local checker (or no checker at all).
LINK_CHECKER_BASE_URL=
LINK_CHECKER_API_KEY=
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID=
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET=
